Z||000003||Master_Sushi||09-23-2001||10:30 AM||||Arn't they one of the earlier parts of a fiero that rusts out? Anyway, nice job! Dosen't look like any water/rust will get in there.<P>Edit- How did you get the carpet out with all the seatbelt hardware bolted on? Just wondering that after looking at the pics again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>------------------<BR>88 Fiero Coupe...<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mesopotamis_1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 09-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Adrift||09-23-2001||12:16 PM||||Why?: Because here in Canada the roads are heavily salted which leads to them rusting away ever year, which allows water to saturate the insulation under the carpet and produce rust.<P>Seatbelts: I had to rip the carpet about 1" in order to get the carpet out without removing the seatbelt ||||reg||1
